---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const base='/equipment/04-11/', oem='https://www.minitech.com/machine-enclosures.html', photo='https://www.minitech.com/uploads/1/1/8/9/118944421/full-enclosure-gx-b_orig.jpg', snf='https://snfguide.stanford.edu/guide/equipment/minitech-gx-micromill-micromill';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Minitech Mini-Mill/GX · closed enclosure and detached drawing" description="Inspect the closed Minitech enclosure and compare two independent authored geometry drawings." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment gx"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/04-11/">← Equipment 04-11</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#gx-evidence">References and verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">04-11 · DOCUMENTARY ENCLOSURE & DETACHED DRAWING / FIRST PASS</span><h2>Minitech Mini-Mill/GX</h2><p>Orbit the closed Minitech enclosure. On the unrelated teaching display, find a circle from three fixed drawing points and check how far a fourth point lies from it. The drawing is not associated with the machine.</p></header>
<div class="grid"><section><h3>Closed, free-standing OEM enclosure</h3><div id="gx-view" aria-label="Orbitable stationary Minitech GX enclosure with four opaque closed leaves and independent exhibit monitor"></div>
<div class="bar"><button data-gx-view="overall">Reset view</button><button data-gx-view="shell">Closed front</button><button data-gx-view="display">Detached display</button><button id="gx-cycle">Switch drawing</button></div>
<p id="gx-ready" role="status">Loading metric model…</p><p>Drag to orbit and pinch or scroll to zoom. The teal button sits on a separate display stand. No front leaf, tool or machine state changes.</p></section>
<section><h3>Detached circle inspection</h3><canvas id="gx-plot" width="660" height="440" aria-label="Synthetic planar sketch with stable points A, B, and C and a held-out point D"></canvas>
<div class="fields"><label>Fixed drawing<select id="gx-mode"><option value="nominal">D on the fitted circle</option><option value="offset">D outside the fitted circle</option></select></label></div>
<div class="bar"><button class="primary" id="gx-inspect">Inspect circle and residual</button><button id="gx-reset">Reset</button></div><p id="gx-status" aria-live="polite">Switch views or inspect the default drawing.</p><output id="gx-result"></output><div class="bar"><button id="gx-json" disabled>Inspection JSON</button></div></section></div>
<section id="gx-evidence"><h3>Geometry and evidence</h3><p>Selected variant: OEM free-standing aluminum-framed enclosure for Mill/2, Mill/3, or Mill/GX, here presented as the GX enclosure option. <a href={oem}>Minitech's enclosure specification</a> gives 45 × 32 × 71 in; its <a href={photo}>front product photograph</a> establishes the four folding leaves, paired lower handles, open base shelf and caster silhouette. The <a href={snf}>Stanford Nanofabrication Facility photo</a> shows a different benchtop housing; it corroborates the separate front-frame treatment, not this floor-standing option's dimensions. Frame details and caster sizes are visually inferred. Real clear acrylic is intentionally replaced with opaque panels, and the interior has no mechanisms.</p>
<div class="grid"><figure><img width="660" height="440" src={base+'front.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original view of freestanding rectangular machine cabinet and adjacent independent display"/><figcaption>Original exterior render, not a photograph. The Minitech description and front photograph anchor the external envelope.</figcaption></figure><figure><img width="660" height="440" src={base+'detail.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original view of four stationary opaque leaves and their dark outer hardware"/><figcaption>Original front comparison with the Minitech product photo, showing fixed opaque leaves and painted stand-in trim.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Independent reference</th><th>Actual / interpretation</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Free-standing shell</td><td>1,143 W × 812.8 D × 1,803.4 H mm</td><td>Verified metric envelope with modeled casters; detached display excluded. Not a measured installation spec.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Detached drawing center/radius</td><td>(16, −12) mm; 50 mm radius</td><td>Recovered from immutable reference points A, B, C.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Held-out point D</td><td>0 mm or 3 mm beyond fitted radius</td><td>The reference circle stays unchanged, while D alone switches between authored variants.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Original register acceptance</td><td>Volume and area from physical-tool motion</td><td>Not implemented or run. No toolpaths, operation, specimens, manufacture or machine control.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>The teaching display subtracts squared distances to derive the two perpendicular-bisector equations. Their solution is the fitted center; collinear reference points do not determine a unique circle. D's signed residual is its distance from center minus the fitted radius. The export records raw points, drawing units and the source revision. No processing, preparation, device settings or material output are simulated.</p>
<p><a href={base+'minimill-gx-static.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={base+'model.py'} download>Editable Blender generator</a> · <a href={base+'circle-example.json'}>Output schema example</a> · <a href={base+'verification.json'}>Verification</a> · <a href={base+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR action contract</a>. No headset or live hardware was tested.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
